For changing global variable value from inside a function
---------------------------------------------------------
a = 10
def greet():
    a = 9
    print("Local variable" ,a )
    
    globals()['a'] = 34
    
    x = globals()['a']
    print("Global Varible", x)

greet()
print(a)


Recursion in Python Function
============================

Recursion means Calling a function from itself.


def greeting():
    print("Hello")
    greeting()

greeting()

If you want to execute some number of time it will execute. it will do continues iteration. by default python will do 1000 times iteration.

For getting the default iteration limit 

>>> import sys
>>> print(sys.getrecursionlimit())
1000

If you want do set the recursion into a specific number ,


import sys
sys.setrecursionlimit(2000)


i = 0
def greet():
    global i
    i += 1
    print("Hello = ", i)
    greet()

greet()



